WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.200
It’s now just four months until MainPower&nbsp;
Stadium opens its doors to the public.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.960
The Mayor, councillors and staff recently visited&nbsp;
the site and were impressed with the progress.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.280
The main court area has seen a dramatic&nbsp;
transformation over recent weeks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.800
following the installation&nbsp;
of acoustic panelling, hoops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.240
scoreboards and the wooden floor&nbsp;
for the four interior courts.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.080
Plywood linings are a feature in many&nbsp;
of the stadium’s rooms and hallways.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.080
Tiling, electrical and plumbing work is also&nbsp;
well underway throughout the various offices,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.480
meeting rooms, bathrooms and gym areas.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:54.960
Outside, the exterior cladding is complete&nbsp;
and beech timber soffits are being installed.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.880
Construction of the eastern car&nbsp;
park is also progressing well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.960
which will provide parking both for&nbsp;
the Stadium and adjacent tennis courts.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.000
Attention now turns to the painting,&nbsp;
interior fit-out and signage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.840
with contractor Leighs on track&nbsp;
to finish construction in July.

